  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:causality_loop_engine",
      "title": "Causality Loop Engine",
      "text": "Entry undated, on purpose. Sends objects back along a closed timelike curve so they exist twice. The universe is not amused.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 5$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "A $(thing)closed timelike curve$() is a path through spacetime that returns to its own past. General relativity allows them in a few exotic solutions; nobody has ever found one in nature.$(br2)This controller is too complex for a crafting grid. Build it on the $(item)Femtoscale Assembly Line$() - check JEI for the exact parts."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "How it works: feed an item together with a $(item)Closed Timelike Curve$() and both come back - plus a second copy of the item. It works on Tesseract Cores, singularities, white hole fragments, superintelligences, stellar cores, wormhole throats and even pocket universes. I try not to think about the last one."
    },
